---
description: Placeholder/mock/dummy data must live in a dedicated data file and be looped, never inlined
globs: **/*.ts,**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: true
---

# Dummy data rules

- Never inline placeholder/mock arrays or repeated fake objects inside components or pages.
- Put mocks in a dedicated module, typed with the real interface from `types/` (or the domain type
  colocated with the feature).
- Prefer existing project locations:
  - `data/<resource>.ts` for general fixtures
  - `lib/<domain>/…` when the domain already lives there (e.g. `lib/user-dashboard/documentRequests.ts`,
    `lib/provider-overview/mockData.ts`)
- Export a named constant (`MOCK_*`, `dummy*`, or domain-specific) — easy to delete when the API lands.
- In UI, always render with `.map()` (or derived lists). Never copy-paste JSX per fake item.
- Keys must be stable (`id`), not the array index, when items have ids.

```ts
// lib/user-dashboard/documentRequests.ts
import type { DocumentRequest } from "./documentRequests"; // or types/

export const MOCK_DOCUMENT_REQUESTS: DocumentRequest[] = [
  { id: "req-1", /* … */ },
  { id: "req-2", /* … */ },
];
```

```tsx
import { MOCK_DOCUMENT_REQUESTS } from "@/lib/user-dashboard/documentRequests";

{MOCK_DOCUMENT_REQUESTS.map((request) => (
  <RequestCard key={request.id} request={request} />
))}
```

## Do not
- Embed multi-item mock JSON in `page.tsx` / component bodies.
- Invent untyped `{ title: "…" }[]` literals when a domain type already exists.
- Leave mocks unnamed (`const data = […]` next to JSX) — export from a data module.
